PREDECESSOR NOTE (honesty): the P1/S8 shared SettingsStore
(io.teslasync.shared.core.presentation.settings.SettingsStore) + its S7
HttpSettingsRepository + the PollingConfig/CaptureStats/VersionInfo/ApiSuspendResult models
already exist on this branch and expose EXACTLY the four reads + two mutations the web page
uses (settings, polling-config, capture-stats, version; toggle-suspend, update-polling-config).
DataContainer already exposes `settingsStore` (it also backs the live unit formatter), so NO
DI-graph widening was needed — the page binds the real shared holder end to end. No predecessor
was stubbed or bypassed; the view performs no HTTP.

NAV NOTE: the `fleetApi` -> /fleet-api destination already exists in Destinations.kt (pre-existing
metadata row, NavGroup.Admin); this prompt only attaches host content via PageHosts.register, and
the deep link is auto-registered by TeslaSyncNavHost.

GATE PATH NOTE: the project Gradle path is ':android' (settings.gradle.kts maps ':android' -> app/);
the prompt snippet's ':app:' is the same module.

STRINGS NOTE (honesty, ADR-014 + no-silent-drift): the web page resolves 70 literal-key strings via
t('Fleet API Settings') etc. 9 already existed in the generated res/values catalog
(translation_Commands/Failed/Nearby_Charging/Recent_Alerts/Release_Notes/Service_Data/common_noData/
enabled/vehicle). The remaining 61 were added to the platform string catalog — the explicit
allowed-files target res/values*/strings.xml — in all three locales (values, values-ar, values-he;
ar/he carry the English fallback exactly as the generator materializes placeholder locales), with
XML-correct escaping (& -> &amp;, ' -> \'). Resource names use the generator's androidName rule
(translation. + key, [^A-Za-z0-9_] -> _) so they match a future gen-i18n pass.

